  (text "BoltATAS v1.1 - review fixes and design notes" (at 20.32 200.66 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0c7e0129-dd3b-42a7-832d-b8f6a47919e1))
  (text "RF path: radio -> J1 -> T1 1T (RF_TX->RF_LINE) -> C1..C3 DC block -> RF_ANT -> J2 -> ATAS-100.\nTandem match (Sontheimer): T1 = current transformer, 30T from GND to FWD_PORT. T2 = voltage transformer,\n30T from RF_LINE to GND, its 1T (coax centre) between FWD_PORT and REF_PORT. Both coax braids grounded at ONE end.\nFWD and REF swapped when testing? Swap the two 30T leads of T1.\nCoupling 20log(30) = 29.5 dB + 13 dB pi-pad = 42.5 dB. 120 W -> +8.3 dBm at the AD8307 (linear to +16 dBm),\n200 W -> +10.5 dBm = 2.36 V at the ADC (ESP32 linear to 2.45 V). Pad = the 50 ohm port load: 78.7 || (105 + 31.6||1.1k) = 49.8 ohm.\nDC is injected AFTER the DC block: it must never reach T2 (its 30T winding is a DC short) or the radio.\nMotor: K1 NC feeds K2 COM, so 12 V and 8 V can never meet; K1 wins. Idle: motor line to 0 V via R41.\nAD8307: OUT unloaded (25 mV/dB, 12.5k internal), ENB tied to VPS, INM AC-coupled, 1 uF on OFS for 160 m.\nL1: 20 turns 0.8 mm CuL on FT114-43 (about 240 uH). Measure |Z| >= 1.5 kohm over 1.8-30 MHz with a VNA.\nRelays: pin numbers per the KiCad SRD footprint (1 COM, 3 NO, 4 NC) - check COM-NC continuity before soldering.\nWT32-ETH01: IO0 is the 50 MHz Ethernet clock input, keep R50 right at the socket. IO5 not used (strapping pin).\nTune only with <= 25 W carrier (firmware refuses above). Heatsinks on U1 and U2 (motor current)." (at 20.32 207.01 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 442ecfc8-bb9b-48d0-a2e7-e8ecdd2a833f))
  (text "A  RF path: tandem match, DC block, bias tee" (at 20.32 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid 7f0c6457-5c33-4133-be80-4b259fc53fbd))
  (text "B  FWD / REF detectors (13 dB pad + AD8307)" (at 20.32 111.76 0)
